  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Western New England University was first established in 1919, and became a university in 2011. Located in Springfield, Massachusetts, the university offers around 50 undergraduate majors and more than 20 graduate programs to students.</p><p>Their main campus is ranked 11th worldwide for being one of the most beautiful campuses to visit, with its first-rate facilities and laboratories. International students are welcomed into a friendly campus environment, where the international population makes up around 5% of the student body.</p><p>The personal values of the university are denoted as integrity, accountability, and citizenship.</p><p>The D'Amour Museum of Fine Arts on campus showcases an impressive collection of visual art, providing an enriching cultural experience. These facilities, among others, underscore Western New England University's commitment to providing a comprehensive and well-rounded education for its students.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>The Quad (Berkshire, Franklin, and Hampden Halls) or Windham Hall, all provide students with traditional first-year accommodation. These residence halls are co-ed, with double rooms and single-sex floors. Bathroom and lounge facilities are shared with other students, inclusive of a kitchenette, television and sofas. Windham Hall offers limited options for triple rooms if any students wish to live in three-person groups.</p><p>Commonwealth Hall, Evergreen Village, Gateway Village, LaRiviere Center, or Southwood Hall are all typically occupied by second-year students, with a mix of other years housed here too.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Lab",
      "value": "<p>The Center for the Sciences and Pharmacy features state-of-the-art laboratories outfitted with advanced equipment, enabling students in the sciences and pharmacy programs to engage in hands-on research and experiments. The campus also boasts a dedicated engineering building, equipped with specialised labs for disciplines such as mechanical, electrical, and computer engineering. The Wellness Center offers a fitness center, indoor track, and multi-purpose courts.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Library",
      "value": "<p>Western New England University offers an array of facilities designed to improve the academic experience. The recently renovated Blake Law Center houses a comprehensive law library, moot courtrooms, and modern classrooms equipped with cutting-edge audio-visual technology.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student Life",
      "value": "<p>Students can check the calendar of events for exciting activities taking place on their doorstep such as Homecoming or Family &amp; Friends Weekend. The student body is also active in creating fun societies such as Model United Nations and Forensic Science Club, for students to pursue their passions and make friends at the same time. 80% of students choose to spend their weekends on campus because of how many exciting activities there are to do.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
  ],
